  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for kubevirt1.9",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for kubevirt1.9 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-13622: virt-handler migration proxy follows symlinks allowing container escape to host (bsc#1272840).\n- CVE-2026-78659: golang.org/x/net/http2: HTTP/2 server memory exhaustion due to Trailer headers (bsc#1286984).\n- CVE-2026-78660: golang.org/x/net/http2: HTTP/2 transport accepts malformed framing-related headers (bsc#1287039).\n- CVE-2026-78663: golang.org/x/net/http2: double flow control refund on HTTP/2 server streams (bsc#1287143).\n- CVE-2026-78669: golang.org/x/net/http2: excessive CPU consumption from repeated initial window changes (bsc#1285255).\n- CVE-2026-97032: golang.org/x/net/http2: HTTP/2 server crash due to HPACK encoder race (bsc#1287446).\n\nUpdate to version 1.9.1:\n\n * virt-template is pinned at v0.2.3\n * several bug fixes, see\n https://github.com/kubevirt/kubevirt/releases/tag/v1.9.1\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
